# Terraform provider sync

VirtFoundry exposes a **REST API** (`/api/v1`). We maintain a first-party Terraform provider that maps API resources to `virtfoundry_*` resources.

**Rule:** every **major new API resource or breaking API change** in `core` must include a matching update in the Terraform provider (same PR or immediate follow-up before release tag).

## What counts as "major"

| Change | Provider action required |
|--------|-------------------------|
| New CRUD entity (new route prefix) | New `virtfoundry_<name>` resource + docs + acceptance test |
| New required field on create | Add attribute; bump provider MINOR if released |
| Renamed/removed API field | Deprecate attribute or bump provider MAJOR |
| New read-only catalog endpoint | Consider `virtfoundry_<name>` data source |
| Action-only endpoint (start/stop VM) | Resource `lifecycle` block, or `virtfoundry_vm` with `state` attribute |

Does **not** require provider changes: UI-only, WebSocket console, internal worker jobs, Helm/chart-only.

## PR checklist (API features)

When adding or changing `/api/v1` resources:

1. Update [docs/TERRAFORM-PROVIDER-PLAN.md](../../docs/TERRAFORM-PROVIDER-PLAN.md) — status column for the resource
2. Implement or ticket provider resource in `terraform-provider-virtfoundry` (separate repo)
3. Add `examples/` snippet under provider repo
4. Mention in CHANGELOG (both repos) when provider ships the resource

## Provider repo (target)

- Name: `terraform-provider-virtfoundry`
- Org: `virtfoundry`
- SDK: [Terraform Plugin Framework](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/plugin/framework)
- Auth: provider block → `POST /api/v1/auth/login` → JWT on requests + `X-Tenant-ID` header

## Resource naming

| API | Terraform type |
|-----|----------------|
| `/tenants` | `virtfoundry_tenant` |
| `/vpcs` | `virtfoundry_vpc` |
| `/networks` | `virtfoundry_network` |
| `/security-groups` | `virtfoundry_security_group` |
| `/volumes` | `virtfoundry_volume` |
| `/snapshots` | `virtfoundry_volume_snapshot` |
| `/vm-templates` | `virtfoundry_vm_template` |
| `/vms` | `virtfoundry_vm` |
| `/vm-snapshots` | `virtfoundry_vm_snapshot` |
| `/ssh-keys` | `virtfoundry_ssh_key` |

Data sources: `virtfoundry_service_offerings`, optional CIDR plan helpers.

## Version coupling

- Provider version follows SemVer independently from app/chart
- Document **minimum VirtFoundry API version** in provider README (e.g. `>= 1.0.0`)
- Breaking API changes → provider MAJOR or documented upgrade guide
